    <item>
      <title>Drawing ChemDraw Chemical Structures with AI LLMs</title>
      <link>/en/chemdraw/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:40:00 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>/en/chemdraw/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;As the title says, here is the situation:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When we use ChemDraw to draw a series of molecules sharing a similar scaffold, copying and pasting SMILES directly, or downloading mol/sdf files straight from the web, often makes it hard to keep their scaffold layouts looking exactly the same. For example, a substituent on the same scaffold is sometimes drawn above and sometimes below; adjusting everything by hand is a real pain.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Searching Compound Information Using ChEMBL Python API</title>
      <link>/en/chembl/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 May 2025 07:58:35 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>/en/chembl/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;introduction&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;ChEMBL is a database beloved by chemistry professionals. ~~~~(Because it&amp;rsquo;s free)~~~~ However, if we want to collect information in bulk, searching individually through the web interface can be quite troublesome. So, is there a method to obtain molecular information &lt;strong&gt;in bulk&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;automatically&lt;/strong&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Actually, besides the well-known ChEMBL &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreffer &#34;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt;, ChEMBL thoughtfully provides a ChEMBL web service client that can be used with Python. By simply entering the desired keywords in Python code, we can search in bulk for the content we need and save it as a CSV file for subsequent processing. ~~~~(For example, cyber alchemy,aka Machine Learning)~~~~&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>InDraw -- Convert Figures to SMILES with AI</title>
      <link>/en/structure-ocr/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 12 Aug 2024 15:00:01 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>/en/structure-ocr/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://indrawforweb.integle.com&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreffer &#34;&gt;InDraw&lt;/a&gt; for web is a powerful online chemical structure drawing tool. It can convert chemical figures (in articles, for example) to SMILES so that we can edit the structures ourselves. Currently, it only supports Chinese. Let&amp;rsquo;s see how it works.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 id=&#34;step-1-register&#34;&gt;Step 1. Register&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img&#xA;        class=&#34;lazyload&#34;&#xA;        src=&#34;/svg/loading.min.svg&#34;&#xA;        data-src=&#34;/img/OCR/1.png&#34;&#xA;        data-srcset=&#34;/img/OCR/1.png, /img/OCR/1.png 1.5x, /img/OCR/1.png 2x&#34;&#xA;        data-sizes=&#34;auto&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;/img/OCR/1.png&#34;&#xA;        title=&#34;Test&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;img&#xA;        class=&#34;lazyload&#34;&#xA;        src=&#34;/svg/loading.min.svg&#34;&#xA;        data-src=&#34;/img/OCR/2.png&#34;&#xA;        data-srcset=&#34;/img/OCR/2.png, /img/OCR/2.png 1.5x, /img/OCR/2.png 2x&#34;&#xA;        data-sizes=&#34;auto&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;/img/OCR/2.png&#34;&#xA;        title=&#34;Test&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;img&#xA;        class=&#34;lazyload&#34;&#xA;        src=&#34;/svg/loading.min.svg&#34;&#xA;        data-src=&#34;/img/OCR/3.png&#34;&#xA;        data-srcset=&#34;/img/OCR/3.png, /img/OCR/3.png 1.5x, /img/OCR/3.png 2x&#34;&#xA;        data-sizes=&#34;auto&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;/img/OCR/3.png&#34;&#xA;        title=&#34;Test&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Draw TRANSPARENT Chemical Structure with RDKit --With Python Code</title>
      <link>/en/transparent/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 12 Aug 2024 14:21:01 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>/en/transparent/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;background&#34;&gt;Background&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s hard to remove the white background of molecular 2D figures created directly with RDKit. They don&amp;rsquo;t look good when placed in PowerPoint. &lt;a href=&#34;https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s13321-022-00664-x&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreffer &#34;&gt;This article&lt;/a&gt; provided a way to make &lt;strong&gt;TRANSPARENT&lt;/strong&gt; ones.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 1&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 2&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 3&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 4&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 5&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 6&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 7&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 8&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 9&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;10&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;11&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;12&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;13&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;14&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;15&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;16&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;17&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;18&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;19&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;20&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;21&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;22&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;23&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;24&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;rdkit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;Chem&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;rdkit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;rdBase&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;rdkit.Chem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;Draw&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;rdkit.Chem.Draw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;rdMolDraw2D&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;rdkit.Chem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;rdDepictor&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;rdDepictor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;SetPreferCoordGen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kc&#34;&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;rdkit.Chem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;rdMolDescriptors&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;rdkit.Chem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;rdFMCS&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;rdkit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;DataStructs&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;io&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;PIL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;Image&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nf&#34;&gt;show_png&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;bio&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;io&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;BytesIO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;img&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;Image&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;bio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    &lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;img&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;smi&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;s2&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;CCCCCC&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;#Take cyclohexane as an example&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;drawer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;rdMolDraw2D&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;MolDraw2DCairo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;mi&#34;&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;mi&#34;&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;#You can adjust the image size&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;drawer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;drawOptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;clearBackground&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kc&#34;&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;drawer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;drawOptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;addStereoAnnotation&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kc&#34;&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;drawer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;DrawMolecule&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;Chem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;MolFromSmiles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;smi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;drawer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;FinishDrawing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;mol&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;drawer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;GetDrawingText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;show_png&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;mol&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Right click and save it, done!&#xA;Cheers!🍺&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
